  "note": "One source of truth for every playable channel. Palettes are lifted verbatim from each channel's own CSS custom properties, not chosen here. 'mominc' is deliberately absent: it is the network hub and narrative front door, not a game. `roots`/`hide` drive play-route isolation (see tv/mount.js). `live` and `identity_api` are OFF switches: every live-mission and identity element on a landing card renders only when its value here is non-empty, so an unconfirmed broadcast can never produce an invented deadline and no form can collect an address there is nowhere to send. Durations are estimates and are flagged as such until a timed pass is run. `status: \"coming_soon\"` (sag, armie) keeps a channel's television slot but generates no play route and drops it from the playable index and the onward cycle. `mission_id` (per game), `api_base` (root) and `live.station` are the same kind of OFF switch: empty means the redeem/tuning feature they feed does not render.",
